  "implemented": [
    "Five fixed Unix npm plans use selected standalone Node and a captured npm CLI entry. Managed prefix/cache and fixed registry/config arguments stay outside caller DTOs; no shell/elevation/global host install fallback.",
    "Actual package name/version/bin metadata, no-follow manifest handles, physical executable receipts, selected Node version output and captured detection must agree before success. Unsupported targets retain honest finite detection results.",
    "Explicit external Pi configuration overrides and nonempty first-install legacy preferences refuse redirection. Managed Pi MCP adapter registration/help/runtime startup proof uses the owned profile root. Existing auth/preferences are never copied or moved.",
    "Actual AgentManager admission/configuration mutation refuses affected live/idle/cached/admitted/queued ownership, rechecks finite affected agent/project metadata/grants through effects and retains a failure fence for uncertain accepted changes.",
    "Accepted process, pipe, file/directory close and callback work remains owned through raw completion; failed exact closes retain handles. Unsafe retired process-group identities are not signalled.",
    "Native physical document ingress stamps a private lease separate from public payloads. Private fixed progress uses matching epoch/document receipts and cannot redirect to a replacement window. Expired bootstrap/listener attempts cannot replace the current receipt.",
    "Exact install requests have 180-second transport deadlines, owner work 150 seconds, child phases 90 seconds and private progress callbacks five seconds. Other transport operations retain 30 seconds.",
    "Default standalone coverage now includes installation and detection-control fixtures; Root verified their real Node children and temporary package trees under bundled Node."
  ],
